.TH YASMV-SAT 1 "September 2026" "yasmv" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yasmv-sat \- SAT solver configuration for yasmv
.SH DESCRIPTION
yasmv uses a pinned, statically linked CaDiCaL 3.0.1 solver.
Native solver output is suppressed. Other than the seed, CaDiCaL uses its defaults.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --sat-random-seed= SEED
Integer in the range 0 through 2000000000. Default: 0.
Fractional, non-finite, negative, and out-of-range values are rejected.
.TP
.B --solver-info
Print linked solver version, signature, verified build revision, and linkage
as JSON, then exit.
.SH MIGRATION FROM MINISAT
All other MiniSat tuning flags are removed. Explicit use produces an error
with migration guidance; remove those flags from scripts.
This includes random-var-freq, random-init-act, ccmin-mode, phase-saving,
garbage-frac, var-decay, clause-decay, luby-restart, restart-first,
restart-inc, elim, rcheck, asymm, grow, clause-lim, subsumption-lim, and
simp-garbage-frac (each formerly prefixed with --sat-).
No approximate parameter translation is performed.
.SH RESOURCE LIMITS
Query budgets accumulate across solves. Propagation budgets measure search
propagations and are cooperative, allowing overshoot between callbacks.
Conflict budgets larger than the native integer limit are also cooperative.
Zero budgets and cancellation prevent conclusive results even for trivial formulas.
The supported yasmv CNF transformation options are unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yasmv (1)
.PP
docs/CADICAL_BACKEND.md and docs/SAT_SOLVER_PARAMETERS.md in the source distribution.
